.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt SSH3-RUST-SERVER 8
.Os ssh3-rust
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3-rust-server
.Nd SSH3 server: user sessions and forwards over HTTP/3 (QUIC)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -bind Ar addr:port
.Op Fl -hostname Ar name
.Op Fl -cert Ar file Fl -key Ar file
.Op Fl -url-path Ar path
.Op Fl -user Ar name
.Op Fl -shell Ar path
.Op Fl -authorized-identity Ar path
.Op Fl -enable-password-login
.Op Fl -gateway-ports Cm no | yes | clientspecified
.Op Fl -permit-open Ar spec
.Op Fl -permit-listen Ar spec
.Op Fl -max-reverse-forwards Ar n
.Op Fl -max-unauth-conversations Ar n
.Op Fl -max-connections Ar n
.Op Fl -max-channels-per-conversation Ar n
.Op Fl -max-incoming-streams Ar n
.Op Fl -max-incoming-uni-streams Ar n
.Op Fl -initial-packet-size Ar bytes
.Op Fl -max-password-failures Ar n
.Op Fl -password-lockout Ar duration
.Op Fl -sftp-jail Cm chroot | lexical
.Op Fl -max-sftp-sessions-per-user Ar n
.Op Fl -handshake-idle-timeout Ar duration
.Op Fl -max-idle-timeout Ar duration
.Op Fl -server-header Ar text
.Op Fl -require-auth
.Op Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
speaks the SSH3 protocol: one QUIC
.Pq UDP
listener carries an HTTP/3 extended CONNECT
.Rs
.%T RFC 9220
.%D October 2022
.Re
to the secret route
.Pq Fl -url-path ,
default
.Li /ssh3-term ,
and every subsequent bidirectional stream is an SSH3 channel.
Shell and exec sessions, direct-tcp and direct-udp forwards, the
dynamic SOCKS forwarding and the in-process SFTP bridge ride those
channels. The client CLI is
.Xr ssh3 1 .
.Pp
The daemon runs as root and, after the CONNECT authentication, drops
every session onto the account of the requested username (initgroups,
setgid, setuid, the home chdir) before any spawn. Public keys
authenticate out of the box: the
.Pa ~/.ssh3/authorized_identities
file or the
.Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
file of the target account, or the files of the
.Fl -authorized-identity
options. Password authentication is off by default: the Basic step
verifies against the unix accounts only when
.Fl -enable-password-login
or
.Ev SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN=1
turns it on, the brute force stays bounded by the per-account lockout
.Pq Fl -max-password-failures , Fl -password-lockout-seconds
and the unauthenticated conversation cap, and the root account never
authenticates by password.
.Pp
The QUIC handshake needs a certificate: on the first start the server
generates a self-signed pair in memory, and the
.Fl -hostname
options (repeated for every name, the addresses included) carry the
subject alternative names the clients validate the certificate against.
The operator's own pair rides the
.Fl -cert , Fl -key
options: a server started with them serves the given files instead of
the generated pair, and the clients pin or trust that identity
.Pq the Fl -ca-cert option of Xr ssh3 1 .
.Pp
Every option below has an
.Ev SSH3_*
environment counterpart (the same name upper-cased, dashes
underscored), read from the conffile
.Pa /etc/ssh3/ssh3-rust-server.env
through the systemd
.Cm EnvironmentFile ;
the command line wins over the environment. The long options are also
accepted with a single dash, the
.Xr flag 1
shape of the Go reference, so its command lines move over unchanged.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -bind Ar addr:port
The QUIC listen address
.Pq default Li 127.0.0.1:4433 ; the Debian unit passes Li [::]:443 .
.It Fl -hostname Ar name
The subject alternative name of the generated certificate, repeatable
.Pq default Cm localhost .
.It Fl -cert Ar file , Fl -key Ar file
The operator's certificate chain (or fullchain) and its private key: a
server started with the pair serves it instead of the generated
self-signed certificate. The two are given together, a lone half
refuses the start, and the sshd shapes
.Fl c Ar file No and Fl h Ar file
are aliases of the same knobs
.Pq a doubled form of one knob, Cm -c No with Cm -cert , is an error ;
.Fl h
is the host key, the usage rides the long
.Fl -help .
The files are read once at startup: a missing or broken file refuses
the start, and a new identity takes a restart
.Pq the reference does not re-read the files either .
.It Fl -url-path Ar path
The secret HTTP/3 CONNECT route
.Pq default Li /ssh3-term .
.It Fl -user Ar name
The user sessions run as when the client does not request one.
.It Fl -shell Ar path
The shell of the sessions; the default is the login shell of the
account.
.It Fl -authorized-identity Ar path
A file with authorized identities (SSH public keys or OIDC entries),
repeatable; without it the per-account defaults are read.
.It Fl -enable-password-login
The password authentication against the unix accounts; off by default,
the safe side of the reference.
.It Fl -require-auth
Reject the requests that carry no valid credentials.
.It Fl -gateway-ports Cm no | yes | clientspecified
The GatewayPorts policy of the reverse (Fl R) listeners, the
sshd_config semantics
.Pq default Cm no :
force loopback binds, allow any bind, or let the client ask.
.It Fl -permit-open Ar spec , Fl -permit-listen Ar spec
The allowed host:port targets of the client-side forwards and the
allowed binds of the reverse listeners
.Pq comma/space separated, Cm * wildcards the host, Cm ! negates an entry; empty: unrestricted .
.It Fl -max-reverse-forwards Ar n
The reverse listeners one user may hold
.Pq default 10 .
.It Fl -max-unauth-conversations Ar n
Conversations sitting unauthenticated before refusals
.Pq default 100 .
.It Fl -max-connections Ar n
Concurrent QUIC connections
.Pq default 0: no limit .
.It Fl -max-channels-per-conversation Ar n
Open channels one conversation may keep
.Pq default 64 , Cm 0: no limit .
.It Fl -max-incoming-streams Ar n , Fl -max-incoming-uni-streams Ar n
QUIC transport limits for the peer-initiated streams
.Pq default 100 .
.It Fl -initial-packet-size Ar bytes
The initial QUIC packet size; the transport floors the value at the
QUIC minimum of 1200
.Pq default 1200 .
.It Fl -max-password-failures Ar n , Fl -password-lockout Ar duration
The password brute-force lockout: the failures per account
.Pq default 10
and the lockout duration
.Pq default 60s .
.It Fl -sftp-jail Cm chroot | lexical
The SFTP path isolation: the per-session child chroots into the home
of the user
.Pq Cm chroot , the sshd model , the default on unix
or the in-process lexical jail
.Pq Cm lexical ; a chroot without a unix platform falls back to Cm lexical .
.It Fl -max-sftp-sessions-per-user Ar n
The concurrent SFTP sessions one user may hold
.Pq default 16 , Cm 0: no limit .
.It Fl -handshake-idle-timeout Ar duration , Fl -max-idle-timeout Ar duration
The QUIC handshake and idle timeouts, the sshd canon
.Pq defaults 120s and 24h : a bare number reads as seconds, the Cm 120s , Cm 2m , Cm 24h shapes ride.
.It Fl -server-header Ar text
The value of the server header of the CONNECT response
.Pq default: the version string .
.It Fl V
Print the version string and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN
1/true/yes/on: the password authentication switch; every other value
keeps it off
.Pq default off .
.It Ev SSH3_URL_PATH , Ev SSH3_PERMIT_OPEN , Ev SSH3_PERMIT_LISTEN , Ev SSH3_GATEWAY_PORTS
The counterparts of the options of the same names.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_REVERSE_FORWARDS , Ev SSH3_MAX_UNAUTH_CONVERSATIONS , Ev SSH3_MAX_CONNECTIONS , Ev SSH3_MAX_CHANNELS_PER_CONVERSATION , Ev SSH3_MAX_INCOMING_STREAMS , Ev SSH3_MAX_INCOMING_UNI_STREAMS , Ev SSH3_MAX_SFTP_SESSIONS_PER_USER
The numeric caps of the options of the same names; a value that does
not parse is ignored with a warning and the default stands.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_PASSWORD_FAILURES , Ev SSH3_PASSWORD_LOCKOUT_SECONDS
The brute-force lockout; the
.Ev SSH3_MAX_PASSWORD_FAILOUT_SECONDS
spelling is the accepted alias of the lockout duration.
.It Ev SSH3_HANDSHAKE_IDLE_TIMEOUT , Ev SSH3_MAX_IDLE_TIMEOUT
The QUIC timeouts of the options of the same names, the durations
.Pq a bare number reads as seconds .
.It Ev SSH3_SFTP_JAIL , Ev SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN
The jail mode and the seconds to drain the active conversations on
SIGTERM before the close grace
.Pq default 5 , Cm 0: close immediately .
.It Ev SSH3_LOG_LEVEL , Ev SSH3_LOG_FILE
The log level
.Pq Cm trace | debug | info | warning | error , case-insensitive, default Cm warn
and the log file. The file is opened in the append mode
.Pq Cm 0644 ;
an unset or empty value keeps the standard error when the run is under
systemd
.Pq the Ev INVOCATION_ID variable, the journal captures it
and falls back to
.Pa /var/log/ssh3.log
otherwise, the shape of the Go reference. The records are one-line
JSON objects
.Pq Li {"level":"info","time":...,"message":"..."} .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/ssh3-rust-server.env
The conffile read through the unit's
.Cm EnvironmentFile ;
every commented variable is shipped in it.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/ssh3-rust-server.service
The systemd unit; the daemon is enabled but not started at install
time.
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/authorized_identities , Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
The per-account public key chains, the native and the sshd
compatibility forms.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3 1 ,
.Xr sshd 8
